---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const controls=[['Authorised information','Restrict retrieval and actions to information the user is allowed to access. Test role and customer boundaries.'],['Source-linked answers','Use approved sources, show conflicting or missing evidence and ask for clarification rather than inventing an answer.'],['Restricted actions','Enforce permissions, validated inputs and approval requirements outside the model. A generated instruction cannot grant itself authority.'],['Meaningful human review','Show the evidence, limitations and proposed action to the person responsible. Keep an override and correction path.'],['Evaluation before expansion','Test realistic errors, misuse, false alerts and important differences across relevant user groups. Set acceptance criteria for the actual task.'],['Monitoring and fallback','Record relevant versions and operational signals, protect logs, and define the owner, fallback and rollback process.']];
---
<Layout title="Responsible AI: guardrails and human review" description="Explore how Soft Task proposes to design AI with approved data, restricted actions, human review, evaluation and operational fallback for each project.">
<header class="solutions-heading wrap"><a href="/services/ai-automation/">AI & automation</a><h1>Useful AI.<br />Clear limits.</h1><p>We design around a defined business task, approved information and clear limits on what the system can access or change. Controls must be implemented and tested for the particular deployment.</p></header>
<section class="wrap"><div class="guardrail-demo" data-guardrail><h2>See where the system should stop</h2><p>A conceptual example, not a live security test or evidence of deployed controls.</p><nav aria-label="Choose an AI request"><button type="button" data-guard-target="evidence" aria-pressed="true">Approved information</button><button type="button" data-guard-target="missing" aria-pressed="false">Missing evidence</button><button type="button" data-guard-target="action" aria-pressed="false">Unapproved action</button></nav><section data-guard-panel="evidence"><h3>Answer with the supporting source</h3><p>Retrieve an authorised, current record, prepare the answer and show the evidence. The reader can verify it.</p></section><section data-guard-panel="missing"><h3>Ask for clarification</h3><p>If documents conflict or essential evidence is missing, expose the gap. Do not manufacture a fact to complete the workflow.</p></section><section data-guard-panel="action"><h3>Block the action and request review</h3><p>A request to change a payment or critical record must pass the actual permission and approval checks. Model text is not authorisation.</p></section></div><div class="guardrail-grid">{controls.map(([title,text])=><article><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="wrap catalogue-bottom"><h2>Evidence matters more than a confidence label.</h2><p>AI can still make mistakes. Citations and a model's self-reported confidence are not guarantees of correctness. We agree domain-specific evaluation and human responsibilities before expanding the system's role.</p><a class="button" href="/solutions/">Explore practical use cases</a></section>
</Layout>
